          "content": "```python\nFor I: Way1:\n(5 × 4) + (4 × 8) = 52\nWay 2:\n2 × (4 + 8 + 4) + (8 + 4 + 8) = 52\n```",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": []
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.219,
            0.429,
            0.328
          ],
          "sub_type": "code",
          "content": "```txt\nFor II: Way 1:\n(8 × 5) + (8 × 6) = 88\nWay 2:\n8 × (5 + 6) = 88\nFind more ways.\n```",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.337,
            0.285,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 42 – 44**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.366,
            0.292,
            0.385
          ],
          "content": "? **Figure it Out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.386,
            0.87,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": "**1. Read the situations given below. Write appropriate expressions for each of them and find their values.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.425,
            0.883,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": "**(a) The district market in Begur operates on all seven days of the week. Rahim supplies 9 kg of mangoes each day from his orchard, and Shyam supplies 11 kg of mangoes each day from his orchard to this market. Find the number of mangoes supplied by them in a week to the local district market.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.522,
            0.883,
            0.579
          ],
          "content": "**(b) Binu earns ₹ 20,000 per month. She spends ₹ 5,000 on rent, ₹ 5,000 on food, and ₹ 2,000 on other expenses every month. What is the amount Binu will save by the end of the year?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.58,
            0.883,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": "**(c) During the daytime, a snail climbs 3 cm up a post, and during the night, while asleep, accidentally slips down by 2 cm. The post is 10 cm high, and a delicious treat is on top. In how many days will the snail get the treat?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.673,
            0.193,
            0.69
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.701,
            0.455,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": "(a) Expression: 7 × (9 + 11) kg Value: 140 kg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.74,
            0.69,
            0.758
          ],
          "content": "(b) Expression: 12 × 20,000 – 12 × (5000 + 5000 + 2000)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.759,
            0.737,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": "Amount Binu will save by the end of the year = ₹96,000"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.779,
            0.86,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": "(c) In the daytime the snail climbs 3 cm up the post and slips down by 2 cm at night."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.817,
            0.823,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": "So, the distance climbed by the snail on the post in full day cycle = 3 – 2 = 1 cm"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.856,
            0.869,
            0.894
          ],
          "content": "∴ The distance climbed by the snail in 7 days = 7 cm The height of the post is 10 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.895,
            0.81,
            0.914
          ],
          "content": "On the 8th day the snail will climb i.e. 7 × (3 – 2) + 3 × 1 = 10 cm"
        },
        {
